{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersExtend","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ComplexDilogBridge","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmLanden","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmBoundary","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmOnCut"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L248-L273","doc":"**`qou-rstq` item 4, all three regimes at once.**\n\n    extend (π²/6) rogersL x = Re (cLiTwoExt x + log x · log(1−x) / 2)\n\nfor every real `x ≠ 0, 1`. The corpus's **piecewise** extension and `Re` of the\n**analytic** Rogers `L` are the same function.\n\n`extended_sum` is stated for the left side; the level-7 bridge computes with the\nright. This is the identification that lets them talk to each other, and it\ncovers **all six arguments** `extended_sum` uses — none of which is `0` or `1`.\n\nThe three regimes needed three different things:\n* `x < 0` — Landen's identity (`landenCombo_ofReal_eq_zero`);\n* `0 < x < 1` — nothing, the series converges;\n* `x > 1` — the inversion identity **on the cut** (`re_inversion_identity`),\n  which in turn needed integrability of `cLiTwoExt`'s integrand at `x > 1` and\n  the branch-point value `cLiTwoExt 1 = π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L241-L246","doc":"**`extend` IS `Re` of the analytic Rogers `L` on `(0,1)`** — where `extend`\nis the identity and the series converges, so nothing analytic is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L228-L239","doc":"On `(0,1)` both logarithms are real, so `Re` passes straight through. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L199-L224","doc":"**`extend` IS `Re` of the analytic Rogers `L` on `x > 1`.**\n\nThe last of the three regimes. `re_inversion_identity` is the only analytic\ninput; the rest is the same log bookkeeping as the `x < 0` case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L183-L197","doc":"`Re` of the analytic Rogers `L` at real `x > 1`. `log x` is real, so it\nfactors out of the real part; `log(1−x)` contributes only its own real part,\nwhich `Real.log` being even renders as `log(x−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.extend_eq_re_cRogersL_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L146-L179","doc":"**`extend` IS `Re` of the analytic Rogers `L`, on `x < 0`.**\n\nThe corpus's piecewise extension and the analytic function agree on the whole\nnegative axis. Landen (`landenCombo_ofReal_eq_zero`) is the only analytic input;\neverything else is log bookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_cRogersL_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L136-L144","doc":"`Re` of the analytic Rogers `L` at a negative real, in real terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_log_mul_log_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.re_log_mul_log_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L124-L134","doc":"**The real part of `log x · log(1−x)` for `x < 0`.** The `iπ` in `log x`\nmeets a *real* `log(1−x)`, so it drops out of the real part — harmlessly, and\nbecause the partner is real, not because the cut was avoided. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.liTwo_eq_re_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.liTwo_eq_re_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**`LiTwo` on `(0,1)` is `Re` of the continuation.** The corpus's `LiTwo` is a\n`tsum`; inside the disc it agrees with `cLiTwo`, which agrees with `cLiTwoExt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.landenArg_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.landenArg_eq","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L109-L114","doc":"`x/(x−1) = (−x)/(1−x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.one_sub_landenArg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.one_sub_landenArg","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L102-L107","doc":"`1 − x/(x−1) = 1/(1−x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.landenArg_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.landenArg_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L95-L100","doc":"For `x < 0` the Landen argument lands strictly inside `(0,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.cRogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoExtendIdentification.cRogersL","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoExtendIdentification.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The **analytic** Rogers `L`, principal branches. ","signatureChunk":0}]}